---
import InfoLayout from '../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
import FirstViewport from '../components/site-standard/FirstViewport.astro';
import Section from '../components/site-standard/Section.astro';
import StatusBadge from '../components/site-standard/StatusBadge.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_URL, buildArticleSchema } from '../utils/seo';

const pageTitle = `Editorial Policy — ${SITE_NAME}`;
const pageDesc = 'CryptoBonusWorld editorial policy: source standards, ranking independence, country evidence, affiliate separation, corrections and AI-assisted workflows.';

const editorialSchema = buildArticleSchema({
  headline: pageTitle,
  description: pageDesc,
  url: `${SITE_URL}/editorial-policy/`,
  datePublished: '2024-01-01',
  dateModified: '2026-08-10',
  authorName: 'CryptoBonusWorld Editorial Team',
  authorUrl: `${SITE_URL}/about/`,
});
---

<InfoLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDesc} canonical="/editorial-policy/" schema={editorialSchema}>
  <FirstViewport
    family="trust"
    container="standard"
    eyebrow="Editorial policy"
    title="Accuracy and evidence come before commercial status."
    lede="The editorial layer decides what can be stated, ranked or withheld. Affiliate relationships are handled separately from evidence and country authority."
  >
    <div class="policy-meta">
      <StatusBadge label="Source-bound" tone="verified" />
      <StatusBadge label="Country-aware" tone="review" />
      <StatusBadge label="Commercially separated" tone="neutral" />
      <span>Reviewed 10 Aug 2026</span>
    </div>
  </FirstViewport>

  <Section container="prose" spacing="standard" tone="primary">
    <div class="cbw-prose">
      <h2>1. Editorial purpose</h2>
      <p>
        CryptoBonusWorld exists to make exchange comparison easier to understand. We publish exchange, offer and country information only to the level supported by the current evidence.
        We do not present the site as financial, investment, legal or tax advice.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Source hierarchy</h2>
      <p>Claims should be traceable to the strongest relevant source available for that claim.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Regulator, government and public-register sources for legal or licensing matters.</li>
        <li>Exchange-owned legal, product, payment, promotion and support pages for exchange-controlled facts.</li>
        <li>Captured evidence with a checked date, limitations and explicit claim references where the product requires freshness.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Other comparison sites, affiliate articles, user comments and AI-generated summaries are not primary authority for exchange availability or offer terms.</p>

      <h2>3. Country evidence is its own editorial decision</h2>
      <p>
        A global exchange page does not establish country availability. An IP location, browser language, region-wide regulation or absence from a restriction list is not enough on its own.
        Country-facing claims are bound to the exact exchange × country pair and keep unresolved limitations visible.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Ranking and affiliate independence</h2>
      <p>
        Affiliate relationships may fund CryptoBonusWorld, but they do not create evidence, approve a MarketProfile or automatically grant a ranking position.
        A commercial route can be valid while the related country claim, bonus amount or local eligibility remains under review.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ranking copy must describe the ranking that actually exists. A global comparison is never renamed as a local country ranking simply because a visitor selected that country.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Corrections and uncertainty</h2>
      <p>
        Missing or contradictory evidence is not silently filled. When a claim becomes stale, materially changes or cannot be reconciled, the affected state is reduced, blocked or returned to review until it is revalidated.
        Confirmed corrections should update the supporting record as well as the public wording that depends on it.
      </p>

      <h2>6. AI-assisted workflows</h2>
      <p>
        AI-assisted tools may help with drafting, structuring, comparison and quality checks. They are not treated as factual sources.
        Public claims still depend on the underlying source and governance rules, and consequential promotion or publication states remain gated.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Disclosure and contact</h2>
      <p>
        Read the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a> for commercial relationships,
        <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> for product evidence rules, and
        <a href="/update-policy/">Update Policy</a> for freshness handling.
        To report a factual problem, use the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</InfoLayout>

<style>
  .policy-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--cbw-space-2); align-items: center; margin-top: var(--cbw-space-4); color: rgba(255,255,255,.58); font-size: 10px; }
</style>
